# What NOT to ship in the .vsix.
#
# This file has to exist. Without it vsce falls back to .gitignore — which lists `out/`,
# because compiled output is a build artifact — so the packager dropped the very directory
# the entrypoint lives in and refused to build with "Extension entrypoint(s) missing".
# The rule is inverted between the two files: git must ignore out/, the package must contain
# it and nothing else.

# TypeScript sources and build config — the .vsix ships compiled JS only.
src/**
test/**
out/test/**
out/**/*.test.js
out/**/*.map
**/*.ts
tsconfig.json
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.gitignore
.vscodeignore

# Dev-only dependency tree; the extension bundles no runtime deps.
node_modules/**

# Build/CI scripts. MEASURED, not assumed: without this line `vsce package` shipped
# scripts/check-vsix-listing.sh inside the .vsix — a CI shell script delivered to every
# customer's install. This file is an exclude-list, so a NEW top-level directory is shipped
# by default; that is the direction it fails in.
scripts/**
